type: generic
title: "Archimedean first-slab positivity for shifted zeta canonical systems: an off-center Weil generator and a radial energy identity"
abstract: >-
  For omega > 0, Suzuki's shifted scattering function Theta_omega admits a
  prime-gamma Hankel kernel. On the prime-free first slab (depth L <= log 2)
  the arithmetic Hankel operator reduces exactly to a reflected finite-horizon
  Volterra convolution with completed-gamma transfer. Differentiating the
  transfer in the shift produces an off-center prime-free Weil form with an
  exact bounded-kernel decomposition. An Arb-certified Legendre calculation
  proves its strict positivity for 0 <= omega <= 1/2, and a shift-energy
  identity converts this into strict contractivity ||V_{omega,L}|| < 1 and
  reflection positivity I +/- H_{omega,L} > 0 throughout the first slab for
  0 < omega <= 1/2. The result is prime-free and finite-depth and proves
  neither the Riemann hypothesis nor a new zero-free region.
